  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "11000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "type": "Output/Note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -380,
      "w": 560,
      "h": 330,
      "state": {
        "Text": "11 \u2014 RUN A GRAPH FROM THE COMMAND LINE\n\nvnoder-cli runs a saved graph once, as Run Once does, and exits:\n\n    vnoder-cli samples/11-command-line.vnoder --name Ada\n\nCLI Param nodes are the graph\u0027s parameters. Run with only the file to list them; a lone -- runs on the defaults:\n\n    vnoder-cli samples/11-command-line.vnoder\n    vnoder-cli samples/11-command-line.vnoder --\n\nCLI Write prints to standard output (or error), and Exit Code sets the code the process exits with, so a script can branch on what the graph found. Without an Exit Code node vnoder-cli exits 0, or 1 if a node failed.\n\nIn the editor there is no console: CLI Write passes its text on (wire it to an Output to see it), and Exit Code does nothing.\n\nTop row: a greeting, a pause, then a second line \u2014 Done \u2192 Run If keeps the three in order. Bottom row: the exit code is 0 when %TEMP% exists, 3 when it does not."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "11000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "type": "System/Machine Info",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0
    },
    {
